{"type":"text","timestamp":1792306018789,"sessionID":"ses_64de1b08cfce4774c9b8","part":{"id":"prt_14dc379e0001ZIkmNt8CYVirng","sessionID":"ses_64de1b08cfce4774c9b8","messageID":"msg_14dc36096001BLQwZYID1CFkiP","type":"text","text":"Checked locally with git 2.54.0 and `opencode run --help`:\n\n- **`git log --max-count`:** there's no default limit, so it shows every commit. `git log --help` doesn't name a default. In a test repo with 30 commits, `git log` without the flag listed all 30, and so did `--max-count=-1`.\n- **`opencode run`:** the agent is chosen with `--agent <nome>`.","time":{"start":1792306018784,"end":1792306018789}}}
